{
  "checked_at": "2026-10-28",
  "ruling": "D0c (owner, 2026-10-28): the integer generation is the major, the latest point ranks, tiers are separate, and the lifecycle status step may activate a row without a benchmark figure. The rules below are encoded in lib/db/repositories/model-lifecycle.ts (MODEL_LIFECYCLE_RULES).",
  "rules": {
    "available": "available is true when, on checked_at, the vendor has not deprecated or retired the model and either its public API docs list the model id as callable (basis api_docs) or its open weights are downloadable from the vendor's Hugging Face org (basis hf_weights; a gated download that needs a licence acceptance counts). A model the vendor has deprecated but still serves is not available. Preview-only, waitlist, consumer-app-only and restricted-access models are not available.",
    "major": "major is the integer generation the vendor markets; the tier line (line, tier) is a separate dimension. Point releases share a major: only the latest available point of each line and major is active.",
    "active": "Exactly one active row per line and major. An active row needs available true, an https availability source and a coding_source_url.",
    "deprecated": "deprecated is the archive: the row stays, keeps its URL and leaves the ranking. archive_reason is superseded (superseded_by names the active row that replaced it) or unavailable.",
    "coding": "coding_source_url names a page that lists the model in a coding benchmark: any Vals coding benchmark page, or for an open-weight model its vendor model card when the card reports a coding evaluation. The Vals Terminal-Bench 4.0 page is the primary source. Only the URL is recorded; benchmark figures stay out of this file and load through the separate metrics step.",
    "scope": "Every model row of the seed files plus the live family rows named in MODEL_LIFECYCLE_LIVE_SLUGS. Image and video models are out of scope (D52)."
  },
  "notes": {
    "history": "Metrics history that D91 folded into claude-opus from the Opus 4.x rows stays on claude-opus; claude-opus-4 starts with none.",
    "redirects": "The status step re-points the opus-4-6 and opus-4-5 redirect aliases from claude-opus to claude-opus-4 (MODEL_REDIRECT_REPOINTS).",
    "archive": "Archived rows keep their tool pages; no archive page exists. Archived point rows are seeded only for superseded points listed on the Vals Terminal-Bench 4.0 page."
  },
